<p>Turkish police fired tear gas and detained hundreds of people during May Day demonstrations in Istanbul on Friday after groups tried to march toward Taksim Square despite restrictions on gatherings there. The Istanbul governor’s office said 575 people had been detained by 6 p.m. local time for defying security decisions, while the ÇHD Lawyers’ Association gave similar figures as the day progressed. Authorities sealed off Taksim Square and set up metal barricades around central districts, including routes through Beşiktaş and Mecidiyeköy, where police intervened. Police used tear gas, pepper spray and, according to several accounts, water cannon as demonstrators sought to reach the restricted square. May Day rallies also took place in other Turkish cities, including Ankara, while official celebrations in Istanbul were held in Kadıköy and Kartal. Turkish reports and opposition footage showed several individual confrontations and detentions during the day.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/-TUsKTbuE05rA21PGV__Y7DjeHGAtUdSuNGX9dOAzazBob6ENMOjnhK7ewLy4zo4qufJQ_gg6qDjGUvOywoebSPdRTijpuCSS0bHlN6YhgfXzFPVK56cYuWfdt4SkBeg7DnSgGeYbDPQ2ciU_YgrLw3vD-kEBndZNvDviFI1_JJaQ5vlYNeBQfSeODiX-isffjzcMV6m_7mNOe_DYvfU' alt='Police detain a demonstrator during May Day events in Istanbul.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Annual policing context: Turkey deploys large numbers of police on May 1 each year, when workers’ and union-led marches are held.</li><li>Count updates: Detention figures rose through the day, from early reports in the hundreds to late official and lawyers’ totals.</li><li>People detained: Reports said opposition representatives, trade-union activists and journalists were among those taken into custody.</li><li>Other May Day rallies: A Czech public broadcaster report noted May Day marches in countries from France to Indonesia and South Korea, with demands including wages, working conditions and peace.</li></ul><blockquote>Those in power already speak 365 days a year, so let workers talk about the hardships they face at least one day a year - Erkan Baş</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Istanbul governor’s office: The governor’s office described the demonstrators as “marginal groups” that ignored security measures and said police units continued processing detainees. (<a href='https://haber.mynet.com/istanbul-valiligi-duyurdu-1-mayis-ta-575-kisi-gozaltina-alindi-110107291548'>Mynet</a>)</li><li>ÇHD Lawyers’ Association: The association provided a non-government running tally from marches across Istanbul, at times putting its figure slightly above the governor’s late-day count. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/turkce/articles/c5ye51e139xo'>BBC Turkish</a>, <a href='http://tr.euronews.com/2026/05/01/1-mayista-taksime-yurumek-isteyenlere-polis-mudahalesi-gozalti-sayisi-350ye-yukseldi'>Euronews Turkish</a>)</li><li>Turkish Workers’ Party leader Erkan Baş: Images aired by opposition channel HALK TV showed Baş being hit with pepper spray as he attempted to march. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996822/hundreds-arrested-at-istanbul-may-day-rallies'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Union official Başaran Aksu: Aksu was arrested after he denounced the Taksim lockdown and said the square was open for official ceremonies and celebrations but closed to workers and the poor. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996822/hundreds-arrested-at-istanbul-may-day-rallies'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/turkish-police-fire-tear-gas-arrest-hundreds-at-istanbul-may-day-rallies/article70929097.ece'>Turkish police fire tear gas, arrest hundreds at Istanbul May Day rallies</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996822/hundreds-arrested-at-istanbul-may-day-rallies'>Hundreds arrested at Istanbul May Day rallies</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy2x7rq3nqo'>Turkish police arrest more than 500 people at May Day rallies</a> - bbc.com</li><